course: dictionary
lesson: 5449
title: Landline
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A landline is a telephone joined to the phone network by a wire. It usually stays in one place, like a house or an office, so it is not the same as a mobile phone you can carry. «A landline phone sends the call along a wire or fibre to an exchange and on to the other phone.» The word line tells you the call travels along a wire.
explain: Landline has a second meaning: it is also the phone number of that fixed phone. When someone says «call the landline», they mean dial the number of the phone in the house, not the mobile. Many children learn their home landline number in case of an emergency.
explain: Context helps you here. Look for clues like wire, house, office or mobile. If a text talks about switching off old copper phone lines, you can guess it is about the wires that carry calls, so landline must be about phones connected by wires.
fact: A landline is a telephone connected by a wire to the phone network.
fact: A landline usually stays in one place, such as a house or an office.
fact: A landline is not a mobile phone.
fact: «Landline number» means the phone number of a fixed phone.
fact: Many homes now have only mobiles, so some families no longer have a landline at all.
exercise: «A landline phone sends the call along a wire or fibre to an exchange.» What is a landline? | A radio that plays music | A phone you carry in your pocket everywhere | A letter sent by post | *A telephone connected by a wire, usually fixed in a house or office
exercise: Mum says, «Call the landline if the mobile is dead.» What does she mean? | Look for the phone in the car | *Dial the number of the fixed phone at home | Post a letter to the house | Send a text message to her mobile
exercise: Which one is NOT a landline? | *A mobile phone you carry in your bag | A phone on the wall in a house | A phone in an office connected by a wire
test: What does «landline number» mean? | *The phone number of a fixed phone | The price of a phone call | The number of your mobile phone | The number of a bus route
test: In «many countries are switching off old copper phone lines», what are the copper lines? | Lines drawn on a map | Mobile phones that are too old | *Old wires that carry phone calls | Pieces of jewellery made of copper
exam: Which best describes a landline? | A computer game | A kind of weather | A mobile phone that fits in a pocket | *A fixed phone connected by a wire to the phone network
